    Validation boundaries:
    
    - **PCP:** the original 2800-second case timed out in earlier runs. The
    later successful job used the same W8A8 weights, DP2 × TP2 × PCP4,
    DSpark and GPQA parameters, with diagnostics disabled and outer/engine
    readiness budgets of 5400/6000 seconds. It became API-ready in
    **19m20s**, below the original 2800-second budget, and completed pytest
    in **49m37s**. The original YAML was not subsequently rerun at that
    revision. The earlier diagnostic-enabled run also
    [passed](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm-ascend/actions/runs/40292393027/job/121472291595),
    with 60m13s startup. Startup variability is not a proven deadlock or a
    resolved single-cause code defect.
    - The 310P passing jobs were run before the experimental non-isolated
    build setting was reverted. Other rows also precede subsequent
    rebases/cleanup. They demonstrate model execution on those recorded
    environments, not final-HEAD installation coverage.
    - The 27B TextVQA result meets its fixed threshold but remains below the
    historical 83.16 score; this is not a claim of identical historical
    accuracy.
    - Some successful runs retain post-test shutdown/resource warnings or
    artifact-upload errors. Passing pytest is not a claim of clean shutdown.
    Several shutdown warnings were also observed in daily v0.31 runs.
    - The initial full batch's three setup-only coverage gaps remain
    excluded; the 15-case rerun table does not establish their coverage.
    
    #### Final revision checks
    
    [Final-HEAD E2E / dual-lane
    CI](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm-ascend/actions/runs/40329082724)
    validates `3414acba`. At this description update, pre-commit and DCO
    have passed; the two CPU-UT lanes are still running. Refer to that run
    for subsequent hardware-shard and final results.
    
    Read-only checks on this revision passed: `git diff --check`, parsing
    all 123 changed Python files, and parsing changed YAML/TOML. Historical
    local isolated checks and hardware results are supporting evidence, not
    substitutes for final-HEAD CI.
    
